      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since this if-else-if statement doesn\u0027t have an \"else\" block, it makes the readers wonder what happens if the screen detection mode is not 1 or 2. Because of the range check on `screen_detection_mode`, we know that cannot happen, but that fact is not obvious here.\n\nThere are several ways to deal with this. I suggest rewriting this statement as follows so that `STANDARD` is the default.\n\n```\n  if (cpi-\u003eoxcf.algo_cfg.screen_detection_mode \u003d\u003d\n      AOM_SCREEN_DETECTION_ANTIALIASING_AWARE) {\n    estimate_screen_content_antialiasing_aware(cpi, features);\n  } else {\n    estimate_screen_content(cpi, features);\n  }\n```",
